From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <149953009+CatPieLeaf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] mm: lru_marie: read the per-memcg counter when reparenting

lru_marie 0.11.1 makes mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size() a switch: with Marie
enabled and an evictable lru it answers from Marie's node-global
NR_ZONE_LRU_BASE total rather than from mz->lru_zone_size, and it
deliberately stops maintaining mz->lru_zone_size ("that counter is left to
legacy/orphan folios only").

mem_cgroup_update_lru_size() is untouched and still writes mz->lru_zone_size.
That is fine for every reader-only caller, but memcg offline reparenting
pairs the two:

	size = mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size(child_lruvec, lru, zid);
	mem_cgroup_update_lru_size(parent_lruvec, lru, zid, size);
	mem_cgroup_update_lru_size(child_lruvec, lru, zid, -(long)size);

so it reads a node-wide number and subtracts it from a per-memcg counter
holding only the dying cgroup's legacy folios. On a 7.2.6 desktop that trips
on the first cgroup teardown of boot:

  mem_cgroup_update_lru_size(0000000043a9708e, 0, -3105): lru_size -3105
  WARNING: mm/memcontrol.c:1503 at mem_cgroup_update_lru_size+0x70/0xf0
  Call Trace:
   lru_reparent_memcg+0x1f6/0x300
   mem_cgroup_css_offline+0x2bd/0x6e0
   css_killed_work_fn+0x4d/0x110

The WARN clamps the child to 0, but nothing clamps the parent: it has
already been credited the whole node LRU total, and that repeats for every
cgroup that exits. lruvec_lru_size() feeds those counters to reclaim.

Add mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size_stock(), which reads mz->lru_zone_size with
no Marie switch, and use it at the two sites that pair a read with an update
-- lruvec_reparent_lru() in mm/swap.c and lru_gen_reparent_memcg() in
mm/vmscan.c. Both now move the stock counter to the stock counter, which is
what they were written to do. Marie's own totals need no reparenting: they
are node-global, and the folios do not change node.

lruvec_lru_size() in mm/vmscan.c is left alone; it is reader-only and wants
the switched value.

Present in upstream lru_marie 0.11.1 and 0.11.1r2 -- neither references the
reparent path at all.
---
 3 files changed

--- a/include/linux/memcontrol.h
+++ b/include/linux/memcontrol.h
@@ -937,6 +937,26 @@
 	return size;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The per-memcg counter alone, with no CONFIG_LRU_MARIE switch applied.
+ *
+ * mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size() above may answer from Marie's node-global
+ * NR_ZONE_LRU_BASE total instead of mz->lru_zone_size, while
+ * mem_cgroup_update_lru_size() always writes mz->lru_zone_size. Any caller
+ * that pairs a read with an update -- memcg offline reparenting does exactly
+ * that -- must use this, or it feeds a node-wide number into a per-memcg
+ * counter and underflows it.
+ */
+static inline
+unsigned long mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size_stock(struct lruvec *lruvec,
+		enum lru_list lru, int zone_idx)
+{
+	struct mem_cgroup_per_node *mz;
+
+	mz = container_of(lruvec, struct mem_cgroup_per_node, lruvec);
+	return READ_ONCE(mz->lru_zone_size[zone_idx][lru]);
+}
+
 void __mem_cgroup_handle_over_high(gfp_t gfp_mask);
 
 static inline void mem_cgroup_handle_over_high(gfp_t gfp_mask)
@@ -1365,6 +1385,13 @@
 		enum lru_list lru, int zone_idx)
 {
 	return 0;
+}
+
+static inline
+unsigned long mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size_stock(struct lruvec *lruvec,
+		enum lru_list lru, int zone_idx)
+{
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static inline unsigned long mem_cgroup_get_max(struct mem_cgroup *memcg)
--- a/mm/swap.c
+++ b/mm/swap.c
@@ -1405,7 +1405,7 @@
 		list_splice_tail_init(&child_lruvec->lists[lru], &parent_lruvec->lists[lru]);
 
 	for_each_managed_zone_pgdat(zone, NODE_DATA(nid), zid, MAX_NR_ZONES - 1) {
-		unsigned long size = mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size(child_lruvec, lru, zid);
+		unsigned long size = mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size_stock(child_lruvec, lru, zid);
 
 		if (!size)
 			continue;
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -4762,7 +4762,7 @@
 
 	for_each_lru(lru) {
 		for_each_managed_zone_pgdat(zone, NODE_DATA(nid), zid, MAX_NR_ZONES - 1) {
-			unsigned long size = mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size(child_lruvec, lru, zid);
+			unsigned long size = mem_cgroup_get_zone_lru_size_stock(child_lruvec, lru, zid);
 
 			if (!size)
 				continue;
